From 705e0838730afcc9cb8618ef495a67705f319bdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergio Marin <sergio.marin@pantacor.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 19:13:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rdawlan: forward-port the vendor driver to 6.6

Compiles and links clean as a built-in. The changes are all well-known
API migrations between 3.10 and 6.6:

- timers: init_timer()/.data/.function -> timer_setup() + from_timer(),
  in the fweh helper, cfg80211 connect/scan timeouts and the sdio
  watchdog;
- cfg80211 ops: add_virtual_intf gained name_assign_type and lost flags,
  change_virtual_intf lost flags, get_station takes a const mac, and the
  key ops all gained link_id;
- cfg80211 calls: inform_bss gained a frame type, disconnected gained
  locally_generated, ibss_joined gained the channel, scan_done and
  roamed take parameter structs, sched_scan_results/stopped gained a
  reqid;
- enums: IEEE80211_BAND_* -> NL80211_BAND_*, STATION_INFO_* ->
  BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_*), IEEE80211_CHAN_NO_IBSS/PASSIVE_SCAN ->
  NO_IR, WIPHY_FLAG_CUSTOM_REGULATORY -> REGULATORY_CUSTOM_REG;
- netdev: last_rx and trans_start gone, netif_rx_ni folded into
  netif_rx, tx_timeout gained a queue index, destructor ->
  priv_destructor, alloc_netdev gained name_assign_type;
- vfs: set_fs()/KERNEL_DS are gone, so the file-backed MAC helpers use
  kernel_read()/kernel_write();
- the driver defined 42 static functions in the kernel's own cfg80211_*
  namespace, which now collides (cfg80211_get_station); they are renamed
  wland_cfg80211_*.

Scope decisions, each marked in the code:

- AP, mgmt-tx, TDLS and scheduled-scan ops are dropped rather than
  ported. They are not needed for a station, and each has a different
  6.6 prototype.
- The BSS/RSSI averaging caches live in wland_iw.c, which this build
  does not include, so the instantaneous RSSI is reported instead.
- The MAC-from-calibration read now goes through the mainline msys
  client added in patch 22 instead of the vendor's plat/md_sys.h. With
  no modem it fails cleanly and the caller falls back to a random
  address -- which is what the vendor system does as well.
- rda_mmc_bus_scan() is dropped and rda_mmc_set_sdio_irq() becomes a
  no-op shim: both were vendor rda_mmc exports. Our host does not need
  the re-scan (the card is already enumerated at boot now that u-boot
  applies the pad map), and SDIO interrupt delivery is governed by the
  driver's own sdio_claim_irq()/sdio_release_irq().

Not yet run on hardware.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local forward-port of vendor driver]
